 "books": {
  "cause": {
   "title": "Notes from the Ash",
   "author": "unknown",
   "pages": [
    "Every terrace of the city once drank from the same cistern. When the lamps were first lit, they were lit from the cistern. When the cistern burned, they all went out at once.\n\nI have only been able to find three lamps that still remember their light."
   ]
  },
  "origin": {
   "title": "Where the Fire Began",
   "author": "A magister's apprentice",
   "pages": [
    "The Magister wanted a brighter city. He asked the lamps for more than they had. They gave it, and then they gave the rest.\n\nThe lens fell first. The fire followed the light along the walls, as a fire does, like it had been invited."
   ]
  }
